"IMPLEMENTED (2026-08-13). AUTHORING: cross-map connections are a pack-level JOIN list (LocationMapConnectionAsset: exit/destination map by name, an anchor per side, both_ways flag); push expands both-ways into two directed rows; LocationMapAsset.connection_names REMOVED. Anchors: Entrance (first main room), Ending (last), Edge (random main), Branch (random extra, main fallback). GENERATION: map instances record their rooms (MapRoomsComponent); each connection leaving a map attaches as PENDING to its resolved exit-anchor room (PendingConnectionsComponent). THE ONE DEMAND PREDICATE (user): an instance is demanded when a player is inside it OR a player shares a room with a path -- materialized or pending -- leading into it; one map_demand_system drives everything: demanded pending connections MATERIALIZE (generating the far map on first demand; path wears the exit map's theme; the return path materializes when the traveler arrives beside the reverse row's anchor); demanded instances shed any cleanup timer; undemanded instances gain a 15-minute map_cleanup_timer (TimerComponent pair) and on expiry -- re-checked against demand -- are torn down: every path pointing INTO their rooms (incl. cross-map paths living elsewhere) deleted, room contents deleted recursively (carried items go with carriers), rooms and instance deleted. Cleaned maps regenerate on demand (checkpoint respawn included -- the loop closes). e2e phase 13-connections (3 tests, real activation flow: walk to anchor -> far map + path appear; arrival -> return path; abandon -> timer, approach the path -> timer shed). Full ladder 0-13 green, 106 unit, clippy 0; dev reseeded -- the meadow->forest->keep->sanctum chain is now actually walkable. OPEN (recorded before): multi-instance resolution still picks the first instance of an asset; instance ownership design pending. Timer EXPIRY teardown is code-reviewed but not e2e-timed (15 min); consider a config knob only if playtests demand it."